title: Payers › List › Search and pick a payer
route: /payers/:id?tab=process
intro: The 'Payers' card on the left: how the rows are grouped, what the dot means, how search narrows the list and what happens when a payer is picked. The tab that was open stays open.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Look at the 'Payers' card\non the left of the page"
screen list "Payers card\n'Search payers' box, then four groups, then a legend"
process grp "Rows sit under four group headings\nOhio Medicaid, Commercial,\nMedicare Advantage, Behavioral carve-out\nA payer added later joins its group"
process row "Each row shows the payer name,\nits plan type and a dot\nSelected row is pale green"
decision dot "Does this payer have a change waiting?"
process green "Green dot\nUp to date"
process ochre "Ochre dot\nChange waiting"
toast tnote "A proposal from Historian alone\ndoes not turn the dot ochre.\nOnly the 'Changes' tab badge counts it"
screen leg "Legend at the foot of the card\n'up to date' and 'change waiting'"

input i1 "Type in 'Search payers'"
process filt "List narrows as you type\nMatches name, plan type or group,\nany capitals"
decision any "Does any payer still match?"
toast empty "No payer matches 'text you typed'."
click clr "Click 'Clear search'"
process clr2 "Search box empties\nEvery payer shows again"

click pick "Click a payer row"
process nav "Address becomes /payers/the-payer?tab=\nSame tab as before. Process if none"
process swap "Header, tab bar and tab content\nswitch to the new payer"
process fresh "Tab content starts fresh\nNo editor, search text or result carries over"
process keep "Search text in the list stays"
click same "Click the payer that is already selected"
process nochg "Nothing changes on screen"
end e1 "The chosen payer's page is showing"

s1 --> list --> grp --> row --> dot
dot -->|No| green --> leg
dot -->|Yes| ochre --> leg
ochre -.-> tnote
list --> i1 --> filt --> any
any -->|No| empty --> clr --> clr2 --> list
any -->|Yes| pick
list --> pick
pick --> nav --> swap --> fresh --> keep --> e1
list --> same --> nochg --> e1
